# `vercel deploy` from a local checkout uploads every file that is NOT listed here or in the CLI's
# short built-in list (node_modules, .next, .vercel, .env.local, .env.*.local, …): it does not read
# .gitignore. Keep local-only files, secrets and agent worktrees out of production uploads (#7).
# Git-triggered deployments only ever see committed files. Tested by scripts/deploy-wizard.test.ts.

# Agent worktrees and per-user settings (each worktree is a whole checkout with its own .env.local)
/.claude/

# Environment files: only the placeholder template is committed
.env*
!.env.example
.mcp.json
*.pem

# Local build output, test results and tool state
/.next-e2e/
/coverage/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/
/supabase/.temp/
/supabase/.branches/
*.tsbuildinfo
